{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/484426-yours-2ed-conditions","id":484426,"title":"Yours 2ED Conditions","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-04-18T05:42:42-07:00","id":484426,"title":"Yours 2ED Conditions","content":"I made a topic about year ago with new Scar mechanics for the game, but now I think better would be just new, with proper 2ED Conditions you make. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Here are mine ideas to use on quasi-Flaws for WtF 2ed games. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <b>Scar (Persistant)</b><br /> It is honorable thing to get scar from memorable hunt in Uratha culture and most werewolves take pride in leaving marks of the previous battles on they flesh, even if they bodies wants to heal them. This character made sure her previous fatal wound, lost organ or ripped off limb healed only enough to show that it was lost. Character can leave Scar on herself after getting the Tilt in battle that would left major wounds, like Blindness, Arm or Leg Wrack. She writes name of original Tilt and enemy that was source of it. So werewolf that lost one eye in fight with Pure writes this Condition as <b>Scar (One Eye - Pure)</b> on character sheet.<br /> <b>Effect:</b> Character takes half of modifiers from normal Tilt (rounded down) all the time from half cured effect. When faced with enemy that made her the Scar, character get's +1 bonus to all action against this particular prey, fueled by the memories of her hunt that left he Scar on her.<br /> <b>Resolution: </b>Character let spend Willpower dot and let her regeneration abilities to heal her scar.<br /> <b>Beat:</b> Character encounters a limitation or difficulty that inconveniences her, streaming from the Scar. Your character speaks or listen to the story of how she got her Scar.<br /> <br /> <b>Anger Issues (Persistant)</b><br /> This particular Uratha is much more prone in to going in Death Rage. Was it very specific First Change, werewolf life related problems or just gens, she much more often can go in to <i>Kuruth</i> when specific Triggers are around. Character denotes what list she adds by writing this Condition as <b>Anger Issues ( &lt;Kuruth Triggers List&gt;)</b>.<br /> <b>Effect: </b>She gets next Kuruth Triggers list, with whole 3 package of Passive, Common and Specific Trigger, that she add to those now having.<br /> <b>Resolution: </b>Character fights with her issues, resolving source of here aggressiveness.<br /> <b>Beat:</b> Character is faced with new list Trigger and enter Soft Rage because of it.<br /> <br /> What do you think about those? Have you got your own?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 09-21-2016, 09:23 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}